Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.95,0:00:17.41,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&}Noah Ararat \N{\fs13}The Wise Prince, Age 12
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.27,0:00:22.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Is something bothering you, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.95,0:00:24.79,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Her name is Gigi.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.79,0:00:26.24,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Gigi?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:29.29,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Oh, u-um...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.29,0:00:31.91,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,The line of people bringing \Nyou birthday gifts
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.23,0:00:35.20,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,still hasn't ended.\NIt's been three days...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.12,0:00:38.74,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's about right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.32,0:00:42.12,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,It lasted a full week last year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.12,0:00:43.60,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,A-A {\i1}week{\i0}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.41,0:00:48.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I can't just receive them \Nand be done with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.99,0:00:52.80,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The item received and its sender \Nneed to be recorded in detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.80,0:00:54.82,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's quite time-consuming.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.70,0:00:59.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But I'm sure Evelyn will take \Ncare of everything just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.65,0:01:03.40,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Gigi, you're on the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.40,0:01:04.91,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Oh! Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.42,0:01:09.92,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Prince Noah, now twelve years old,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.18,0:01:14.34,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,has been recognized for fully mastering \Nthe magic sword Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.81,0:01:18.85,italicstop,Narrator,0,0,0,,By direct imperial order, he is stationed\Nat the Ministry of Military Affairs,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.17,0:01:18.84,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\b1\fnTimes New Roman\fs15\fade(238,0)\bord0.25\shad1.5\an2\pos(320,311.333)\c&HE6EDF3&\3c&H676C6B&\4c&H343C3B&}Ministry of Military Affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.85,0:01:21.25,italicstop,Narrator,0,0,0,,which presides over the imperial army.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.92,0:01:26.56,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And serving as its minister is...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.47,0:01:29.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.85,0:01:31.60,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Good. Enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.32,0:01:43.66,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&}Henry Ararat \N{\fs13}Minister-Prince of Military Affairs, Fourth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.94,0:01:44.03,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,There you are, Noah. I've been waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.42,0:01:48.00,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Good morning, Wise Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.00,0:01:48.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.26,0:01:52.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I was told that you wished \Nto see me, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.89,0:01:53.80,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.26,0:01:56.89,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,I wanted to ask your opinion.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.39,0:01:59.73,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,We've received an imperial command
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.73,0:02:02.67,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,to have Reiss here lead a force
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.67,0:02:05.84,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,to suppress a rebellion \Nat the southern border.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.20,0:02:09.30,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,If those barbarians are shown \Nany compassion, they get cocky.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.84,0:02:12.71,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,So we're to dispatch a regular army
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.71,0:02:15.31,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,to show them how much \Ngreater our strength is.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.31,0:02:16.64,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.53,0:02:19.33,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Reiss Keiki, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.74,0:02:24.20,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0.75\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HF6FBF9&\3c&H797A7A&}Reiss Keiki \N{\fs13}Direct Subordinate of the Fourth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.84,0:02:22.30,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Aside from his many acts of valor,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.30,0:02:24.56,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,he's more than talented \Nenough to lead an army.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.56,0:02:28.65,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Even among all of my brother's \Nknights, he is exceptional.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.26,0:02:31.16,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Tell me just one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.16,0:02:34.16,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Of course. Please, ask me anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.35,0:02:37.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,How many soldiers are there, {\i1}truly{\i0}?
Dialogue: 1,0:02:58.57,0:03:00.57,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\c&H4F7C81&\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\pos(320,142.5)}Born Blessed, So I'll Obtain Ultimate Power
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.57,0:03:00.57,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\p1\bord2\c&H291505&\alpha&H255&\3c&H2986A5&\fscx87\pos(311,141.167)}m 0 0 l 235 0 l 225 8 l 235 15 l 18 15 l 30 8 l 18 0
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.77,0:04:15.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.32,0:04:19.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I asked you how many soldiers\Nyou'll be leading.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.10,0:04:23.90,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Th-That is, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.38,0:04:27.94,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,What do you mean by "truly," Noah?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.49,0:04:30.12,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Reiss!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.62,0:04:32.03,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,What are you hiding?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.23,0:04:38.45,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,P-Please forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.94,0:04:43.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Brother, it's not a serious matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.93,0:04:48.25,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But imperial forces receive funding\Nfrom the Ministry of Military Affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.25,0:04:51.55,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,based on how many soldiers \Nare registered, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.55,0:04:52.38,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.14,0:04:56.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And it's common for generals \Nto register non-soldiers,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.17,0:04:58.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,such as merchants and collaborators,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.52,0:05:02.60,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and keep the excess \Nfunding for themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.87,0:05:04.57,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,I sincerely apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.57,0:05:06.03,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Why, you...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.03,0:05:07.74,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Please wait a moment, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.19,0:05:09.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And Reiss, stop cowering.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.30,0:05:13.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's within a general's authority \Nto add new soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.76,0:05:15.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm not trying to place blame.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.92,0:05:18.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Normally, that would be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.14,0:05:22.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Registering soldiers in name \Nonly can serve as a deterrent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.99,0:05:24.02,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.02,0:05:26.48,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Sometimes it's better to say
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.48,0:05:29.99,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,you have an army of 100,000, even \Nif that isn't the actual number.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.99,0:05:31.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Precisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.51,0:05:33.27,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You understand these matters well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.53,0:05:34.91,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Brilliant as always, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.64,0:05:37.70,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But this occasion is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.29,0:05:41.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The emperor's order was \Nfor a sweeping victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.55,0:05:44.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's why I asked about the \Nextent of your embellishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.44,0:05:46.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Answer me honestly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.95,0:05:50.32,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,A-Around two thousand, I believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.75,0:05:53.37,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Then make sure you can \Nactually supply that many.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.37,0:05:55.80,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, Your Highness. At once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.80,0:05:57.78,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,May I borrow a pen and paper?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.78,0:05:58.66,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.30,0:06:05.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Take this to the Ministry \Nof Military Affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.63,0:06:11.31,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,They'll supply enough to cover two\Nthousand more as miscellaneous expenses.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.31,0:06:12.82,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The excess is yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.82,0:06:14.48,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.48,0:06:16.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Take it. And in return...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.55,0:06:20.41,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I will {\i1}not{\i0} tolerate defeat. Understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.20,0:06:22.69,Default,Reiss,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.99,0:06:24.34,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.23,0:06:27.95,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,What masterful usage of \Nthe carrot and stick.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.21,0:06:36.84,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,By the way, Noah...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.33,0:06:41.24,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,you haven't experienced \Nwar yet, have you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.24,0:06:42.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.57,0:06:45.41,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Even at age twelve,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.41,0:06:47.59,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm still at Level 1.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:45.42,0:06:50.63,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs14\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFCF4&\3c&HCDAFA0&\bord0.75\blur1\b1\shad1\4c&H7D605F&\pos(14,20)}Name: Thirteenth Imperial Prince Noah Ararat \NSex: Male \NTitle: Wise Prince \NLevel: 1\h/\h∞ \NHP: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFire: F \NMP: F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWater: E+S\NStrength: F+E\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWind: F\NStamina: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hEarth: F\NIntelligence: F+F\h\h\h\h\hLight: F \NSpirit: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDark: F \NSpeed: F+F
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.42,0:06:50.63,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&H392E2D&\3c&HF8D6AE&\4c&HB7775D&}m 0 0 l 265 0 265 73 0 73
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.00,0:06:50.26,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That's the rule of the imperial family.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.04,0:06:53.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Many royal babies die prematurely,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.94,0:06:57.18,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,meaning they don't survive \Nlong after birth.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.68,0:07:00.45,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Officially, it's attributed \Nto an epidemic,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.45,0:07:03.14,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but most of them are identified \Nas murder by poison
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.14,0:07:05.28,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,by those competing for more power.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.90,0:07:09.54,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Either way, a prince is \Na valuable living heir.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.54,0:07:11.64,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,They aren't permitted to go to battle
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.64,0:07:14.57,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,until they've grown to adulthood, \Nexcept by imperial order.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.12,0:07:17.05,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You're twelve now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.57,0:07:20.34,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Wouldn't it look better if \Nyou got some experience now,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.34,0:07:22.02,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,before you start ruling your fief?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.61,0:07:25.62,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If the emperor orders me to \Ngo, I'll go at any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.87,0:07:29.48,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You have a magic sword. I doubt \Nyou would have much difficulty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.48,0:07:32.15,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,When was your first campaign, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.10,0:07:34.76,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Oh, me? I—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.90,0:07:40.15,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,What's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.15,0:07:41.82,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,Please help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.63,0:07:47.36,Default,Slaver1,0,0,0,,Hold up, damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.36,0:07:48.83,Default,Slaver2,0,0,0,,You stupid brats!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.83,0:07:51.18,Default,Slaver3,0,0,0,,You're nothing but trouble!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.18,0:07:53.30,Default,Slaver2,0,0,0,,It's no use trying to run!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.30,0:07:55.45,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,Someone, please help!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.00,0:07:57.57,Default,Slaver1,0,0,0,,All right, come with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.57,0:07:59.53,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.85,0:07:59.79,top,Noah,0,0,0,,Stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.53,0:08:03.44,Default,Slaver1,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.44,0:08:07.30,Default,Slaver2,0,0,0,,Little brat! Keep your nose \Nin your own business!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.30,0:08:08.53,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Where's your registration?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.53,0:08:09.41,Default,Slaver1,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.41,0:08:11.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Where's your registration? \NYour documents?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.76,0:08:13.84,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is the name of your business?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.92,0:08:16.21,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Answer me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.21,0:08:19.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You know that unregistered slave \Ntrading is a serious crime
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.94,0:08:21.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,under imperial law, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.27,0:08:24.66,Default,Slaver1,0,0,0,,Sh-Shut up, you stupid brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.66,0:08:25.86,Default,Slaver3,0,0,0,,Get him!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.91,0:08:41.00,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.32,0:08:42.23,Default,OnlookerA,0,0,0,,Wow...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.23,0:08:43.27,Default,OnlookerB,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.27,0:08:45.83,Default,OnlookerC,0,0,0,,He handled himself like \Na real sword master!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.53,0:08:48.80,Default,OnlookerD,0,0,0,,What household does he belong to?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.34,0:08:50.84,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.75,0:08:53.71,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,Y-Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.71,0:08:56.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,These are underground\Nslave traders, yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.48,0:09:02.30,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,They said... we'd be worth good money...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.93,0:09:06.79,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,That's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.91,0:09:13.00,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,What a pleasure it is to \Nmeet you, Wise Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.54,0:09:18.33,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,I make my living off of kids \Nlike the ones you see here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.33,0:09:19.48,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,My name is...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.07,0:09:22.68,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,On second thought,\Nperhaps I shouldn't tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.68,0:09:23.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.58,0:09:30.54,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,Because I work for First Prince Gilbert.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.42,0:09:30.54,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&}Gilbert Ararat \N{\fs13}First Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.54,0:09:32.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The first prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.65,0:09:33.75,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.13,0:09:36.24,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Not only does he know who I am,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.24,0:09:41.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but he's threatening me not to meddle \Nbecause he has Gilbert's backing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.16,0:09:50.72,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,I don't want to make waves here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.72,0:09:53.70,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,Please, just pretend you \Nnever saw any of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.00,0:09:56.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Brother, do you know this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.25,0:09:58.12,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.77,0:10:00.86,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.18,0:10:04.61,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,My brother Henry says \Nhe doesn't know you,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.61,0:10:06.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,nor do I.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.08,0:10:08.10,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,But of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.10,0:10:10.17,Default,Boss,0,0,0,,A man such as I would not—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.91,0:10:18.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I swear...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.31,0:10:23.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The nerve of this scoundrel to falsely \Nclaim he serves the first prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.08,0:10:27.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He may have fooled others, but my \Nbrother and I will not be fooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.30,0:10:29.85,Default,OnlookerA,0,0,0,,What? So he was a fake?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.85,0:10:32.26,Default,OnlookerB,0,0,0,,And... who are those two, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.26,0:10:33.55,Default,OnlookerC,0,0,0,,I know them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.90,0:10:38.13,Default,OnlookerC,0,0,0,,That's the songstress Alichey's patron,\Nthe Wise Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.13,0:10:39.68,Default,OnlookerD,0,0,0,,So he's real?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.68,0:10:42.10,Default,OnlookerD,0,0,0,,And the others are the fakes?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.99,0:10:46.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Apprehend these men and take them \Nto the first prince's estate.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.08,0:10:53.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Explain that they are scoundrels who \Nfalsely claimed to work for Gilbert.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.48,0:10:54.43,Default,Drivers,0,0,0,,At once.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.83,0:10:58.37,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Bring the children to my mansion for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.37,0:11:00.13,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll hear their stories later.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.49,0:11:02.89,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Well done, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.37,0:11:04.85,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You handled that brilliantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.85,0:11:07.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm glad it all worked out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.72,0:11:12.02,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If they did work for Gilbert,\NI couldn't kill them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.74,0:11:15.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But if I'd left them \Nto their own devices,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.51,0:11:19.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,the people would think I allowed \Nunderground slave trading to happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.83,0:11:21.91,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's best if I made them out to be fakes,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.91,0:11:25.28,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and let Gilbert handle them himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.72,0:11:31.84,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,The way you do things always \Nsurprises and amazes me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.24,0:11:43.45,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.29,0:11:46.32,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.16,0:11:50.79,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,What is it, Noah?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.79,0:11:54.83,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A messenger of\NFirst Prince Gilbert was here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.83,0:11:57.47,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Oh? What did he say?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.47,0:11:59.27,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,"Thank you for catching them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.95,0:12:02.13,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I interrogated the slave traders,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.13,0:12:05.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and they were indeed falsely claiming \Nmy name to run their business.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.45,0:12:08.54,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I intended to send them to \Ncourt as soon as tomorrow...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.83,0:12:13.24,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but they committed suicide \Nwhile my back was turned."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.95,0:12:15.22,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.72,0:12:17.07,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Honestly...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.52,0:12:19.66,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And people are supposed \Nto be treasures...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.72,0:12:24.28,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,These words must have crossed \Nmy brother's mind as well:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.63,0:12:26.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,"The lizard has shed its tail."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.56,0:12:32.19,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Gilbert ordered those men to run the \Nunderground slave trade, didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.19,0:12:33.27,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.27,0:12:36.70,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,He has absorbed himself in acquiring \Nshops, buying private estates,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.70,0:12:39.48,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,and senseless activities \Nlike that for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.48,0:12:41.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You can't blame him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.05,0:12:41.98,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.07,0:12:46.49,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(983,3145)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs13\c&H3A494D&\3c&HE1E5E7&\frx28\fry8\move(525,158,545,355,0,4404)}Fourteenth Prince \NGary
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.07,0:12:49.70,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(983,3145)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs13\c&H3A494D&\3c&HE1E5E7&\frx28\fry8\move(515,50,545,360,0,7630)}Fourth Prince \NHenry
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.61,0:12:49.70,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(983,0)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs13\c&H3A494D&\3c&HE1E5E7&\frx28\fry8\move(497,-20,520.333,242.333,0,7090)}Third Prince \NKilo
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.98,0:12:47.33,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Gilbert may be the first prince, \Nbut he's a concubine's son.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.03,0:12:49.70,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(983,0)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs13\c&H3A494D&\3c&HE1E5E7&\frx28\fry8\move(490,-20,504,137,0,4670)}Crown Prince, Second Prince \NAlbert
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.33,0:12:48.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He can't succeed the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.62,0:12:49.70,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(983,0)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs13\c&H3A494D&\3c&HE1E5E7&\frx28\fry8\move(481,-20,486.667,47.667,0,2065)}First Prince \NGilbert
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.70,0:12:52.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Perhaps, to vent his frustration,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.06,0:12:55.27,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,he's looking for something he can \Ndo without succeeding the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.27,0:12:59.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The slave trade and\Nprivate estates are just proxies.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.78,0:13:02.11,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You even know that?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.53,0:13:04.72,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,You never cease to amaze me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.84,0:13:08.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Anyone could figure it out \Nwith a bit of thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.83,0:13:11.98,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,No, not exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.81,0:13:15.12,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,This whole thing nauseated me,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.69,0:13:18.32,Default,Henry,0,0,0,,but I feel a bit better now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.11,0:13:23.98,sign_generic,EPTitle,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,0)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 205)}Episode 6
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.11,0:13:23.98,sign_generic,EPTitle,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,0)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 225)}Dark Clouds
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.51,0:13:27.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've pulled some strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.30,0:13:31.55,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,None of you will ever be sold.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.17,0:13:35.21,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You're all free now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.86,0:13:39.00,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Is this what I think it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.00,0:13:40.60,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Do you have anywhere to go?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.65,0:13:43.08,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.08,0:13:48.25,Default,GirlB,0,0,0,,I was sold in exchange for money \Nto buy this year's seed rice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.25,0:13:50.88,Default,BoyA,0,0,0,,I was sold to pay for \Nmy mother's funeral.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.88,0:13:52.44,Default,BoyB,0,0,0,,One less mouth to feed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.44,0:13:54.55,Default,BoyC,0,0,0,,My dad really likes to gamble.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.55,0:13:57.28,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,As I suspected.\NThey have no home to return to.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.28,0:14:00.98,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And with parents like that, if they did \Ngo home, they'd just be sold again.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.54,0:14:02.27,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Dylan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.73,0:14:03.72,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.72,0:14:06.19,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll take them in.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.65,0:14:09.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Find them jobs and places to sleep \Nwherever available.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.48,0:14:13.32,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And if any wish to study, \Nhelp them do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.70,0:14:16.61,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Understood. As always, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.06,0:14:21.12,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,Y-You're going to buy us?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.43,0:14:23.91,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm not buying you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.43,0:14:28.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you want to leave,\Nyou're free to do so at any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.13,0:14:33.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But the one thing I won't \Ntolerate is betrayal.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.38,0:14:38.48,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Is that too difficult for them?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.48,0:14:43.65,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Be grateful for His Highness's\Nkindness and do the best you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.02,0:14:45.83,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Thank him, quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.83,0:14:48.03,Default,GirlA,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.56,0:14:48.03,top,Kids,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.63,0:14:54.04,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,People are treasures, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.09,0:14:58.36,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Oh, that's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.78,0:15:06.34,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,You called, Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.93,0:15:11.74,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,All of your birthday gifts have \Nbeen handled without incident—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.74,0:15:12.84,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No need to report that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.55,0:15:15.22,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It is already apparent.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.09,0:15:21.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Evelyn, I brought this for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.00,0:15:24.29,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.29,0:15:25.46,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your dismissal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.03,0:15:29.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'd like you to be the administrator \Nof a small region within Almeria.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.46,0:15:30.81,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,Administrator?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.24,0:15:35.07,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes. Now you're also a proper \Ngovernment official.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.07,0:15:37.07,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,B-But I...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.58,0:15:42.18,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,An administrator is a key office,\Nalso popularly known as a magistrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.18,0:15:45.55,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,This is a major promotion for a maid.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.04,0:15:50.06,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The fief that the prince received \Nfrom the emperor is vast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.06,0:15:53.47,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,It would be impossible for him \Nto rule over it all himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.90,0:15:59.31,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,So he has assigned administrators to \Nvarious regions to act as his proxies.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.52,0:16:05.40,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've been watching you for many years, \Nand you're the most clever of my maids.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.97,0:16:11.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I felt that just taking care of guests at \Nthis mansion is a waste of your talents.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.23,0:16:15.15,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,B-But... that is... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.47,0:16:20.05,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,I-I would rather keep working for you
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.05,0:16:22.72,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,than go out there and \Nmove up in the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.72,0:16:24.02,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.98,0:16:26.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But you can, and will, grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.22,0:16:31.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you'll work for me as an administrator,\Nit will be known that I,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.30,0:16:33.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,the one who appointed you,\Nam an excellent judge of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.22,0:16:36.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Evelyn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.60,0:16:40.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Leave this mansion and work for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.23,0:16:44.47,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,For... you...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.82,0:16:51.69,Default,Evelyn,0,0,0,,A-All right! I understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.03,0:16:52.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.21,0:16:59.61,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.61,0:17:00.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.65,0:17:02.26,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,It's obvious!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.26,0:17:05.89,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,The way you put people to use is \Nnothing like how the first prince—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.89,0:17:06.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Shirley.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.29,0:17:09.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That is not something you \Nshould say aloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.38,0:17:13.31,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,R-Right. I apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.06,0:17:20.21,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.56,0:17:22.23,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,he really is amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.97,0:17:27.45,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I've heard the story, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.05,0:17:31.76,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You managed to defend Gilbert's honor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.76,0:17:33.54,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It was coincidental.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.29,0:17:37.11,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I merely captured people \Nwho were breaking the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.11,0:17:39.92,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,So my brother reported it himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.92,0:17:41.13,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Smart.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.13,0:17:45.54,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Instead of keeping secrets, he's made \Nit appear as if his hands are clean.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.08,0:17:49.58,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Still, to think such \Nscoundrels were out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.58,0:17:53.09,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What sort of crime is underground \Nslave trading, again?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.09,0:17:55.28,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In cases of unregistered slave trading,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.28,0:17:57.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,the ringleader's dominant \Narm is to be severed,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.56,0:18:00.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and any others involved are \Ndrafted into military service.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.89,0:18:04.23,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Is that correct, First Prime Minister?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.63,0:18:07.65,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,It is precisely as His Highness says.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.60,0:18:12.68,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Oh, right. Were you hurt in any way?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.68,0:18:16.47,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I hear the criminals flew into \Na rage and attacked you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.47,0:18:19.37,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thankfully, I was able to \Nturn the tables on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.37,0:18:22.48,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I suppose, since it's you, \NI didn't even need to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.48,0:18:24.84,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Had it been me,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.84,0:18:28.28,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I would have been undercover, \Nso I may have been defeated
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.28,0:18:31.44,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,while debating whether \Nto reveal my identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.44,0:18:34.43,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,That would amount to a crime \Nagainst the imperial family,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.43,0:18:36.26,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,punishable by death.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.44,0:18:41.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.92,0:18:46.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Under imperial law, if the criminal does \Nnot know His Majesty's identity—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.03,0:18:50.24,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,in other words, if he is undercover \Nand has not yet named himself—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.24,0:18:52.57,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,there is no crime against \Nthe imperial family.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.57,0:18:54.88,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It is treated merely as assault.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.23,0:18:58.65,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Did I go too far?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.63,0:19:04.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,What is or isn't considered rude to say \Nto the emperor is a delicate matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.05,0:19:07.51,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,If he was merely being hypothetical,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.51,0:19:10.42,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,perhaps I shouldn't have \Npointed out his mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.42,0:19:12.87,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It's always best to speak the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.31,0:19:16.88,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but not when it makes a \Nprime minister look bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.88,0:19:18.25,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Should I apologize?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.62,0:19:26.11,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Well, I'd say I won that bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.11,0:19:28.69,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,Yes. I underestimated him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.13,0:19:32.40,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Um... what does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.40,0:19:37.09,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Oh, I just had a little bet going \Nwith the first prime minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.09,0:19:41.34,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It was a test to see whether or \Nnot you could describe the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.34,0:19:42.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,O-Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.86,0:19:45.82,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,A test? But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.82,0:19:50.76,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I have always known that you were strict \Nand impartial in matters of law.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.76,0:19:54.27,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I was testing that, just to make sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.71,0:19:56.34,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.60,0:20:00.73,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,In the name of the Emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.73,0:20:04.69,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I hereby appoint Noah Ararat \Nour minister of justice!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.64,0:20:08.39,Default,SpectatorA,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.39,0:20:12.43,Default,SpectatorB,0,0,0,,Now he's the second minister-prince \Nafter the Fourth Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.71,0:20:16.13,Default,SpectatorB,0,0,0,,Long live Noah,\NMinister-Prince of Justice! Banzai!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.13,0:20:23.07,Default,Spectators,0,0,0,,Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.02,0:20:35.30,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,All I did was answer the way I always do,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.30,0:20:37.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,and I was made minister of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.25,0:20:43.17,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Am I making too much of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.75,0:20:46.74,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Or was there something else \Nbehind this decision?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.54,0:20:55.86,Default,GuestB,0,0,0,,I can see why she's the most popular \Nsongstress in the empire right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.86,0:20:57.78,Default,GuestC,0,0,0,,What a beautiful voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.78,0:20:59.81,Default,GuestD,0,0,0,,I feel like my heart is being cleansed.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.45,0:21:05.77,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,True. Maybe it's inelegant to \Nthink about that right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.55,0:21:17.05,Default,Kids,0,0,0,,It's so good!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.21,0:21:55.00,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, it seems the \Nreport was indeed true.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.37,0:21:57.92,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.11,0:22:00.94,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I'll let you handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.57,0:22:03.30,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,It will be done.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.05,0:22:08.34,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It seems time will wait no longer.
